<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman–Hungarian wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1366–<a href="/years/1526">1526</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman–Hungarian wars were the conflicts between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> from the late 14th century to 1526. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusades</a> against the Ottomans that ended in defeat at Nicopolis (1396) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a> (1444), while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hunyadi">John Hunyadi</a> relieved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> in 1456. The wars ended with the Hungarian defeat at Mohács in 1526, after which most of Hungary was divided between the Ottomans and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottoman-hungarian-wars.jpg" alt="Ottoman–Hungarian wars" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes de Thurocz Stanisław Chlebowski Bertalan Székely · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ottoman-Hungarian_Wars.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
